<description>&lt;p&gt;Algerian troops have arrived in Niger to protect energy assets amid a surge of attacks by jihadist groups, while Niger security forces faced a deadly NSCDC cell incident that killed 14 children among 33 detainees. Russian-affiliated forces in Mali continue killing civilians, and Russia hosted an African leaders summit to deepen ties, prompting Putin to seek expanded relations with African countries. Niger accused Chad of a drone strike that killed two civilians, and a convoy carrying Governor Bago crashed, killing four students, a driver and a young woman. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxNbTFGZkdPQW9jLVZKcU03dE92NVI4d09jLWgwUjBJOWFGVndjS2JaNjlzWVdFcmZUSlRCY0dEcTI4YTFVeXdyLVZKd1JZLUZKNGNiUG1US1ZMZU9ySWY5bnkxNlFpZzMzbFpvc08wQURrYjRVeFVKMmRsdnY4QXVKdjFCcklVT2FkRmRscms4dGNRQ1JUQTdqeW9FcHhMazdIVDA0V25BWXItOFJQNVNXUDBsdGpsMDQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxOUlpTd0ZNX1ZMR0tpUFlwSlJKWEt1bU5MemhMU2xvZS1WVnpzeXRLcGNlaWpqZ1pLb0ZwZkUtTXhHZTVPNnphNWVLZFJEdnJLMURIZXpKdGc0azVETkREMzZwY3RDNXFxQ0toWm5YejkwWDI4N0RFNHljbW9pV3ZkVWpvcC0yTDE3QlN5X3BudVNEWHRMOTdyTHZFTlVzTnNONmYzU0hwN0RRaEhHUzBlWFk0WDhsV1dzcUhxNXI1SjYzV28?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxPVU5UZ2w5YVgxcmV4aUswWEhzbXN4T0E5MkNmMldSRVVsSzFocE01clctNUlzSlc0Z1FkLVp1aVNXTlgwejNILW1LT3JwbGNFTjlaanFSNHM0TGZ5V0Njc2FQMTd1SVhfNkMteDlub2MwTGFNdkZfQ1Y5YnpvaGxxa0o2VndDaFNHakg5M3VJdVJ2elkwQS1pSU05Z09DTDNKaEdvcjB5TDVnV2c?oc=5&quot;&gt;Egypt Independent&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Tribune Online&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Dubawa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a h